  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 with George F. Root's original 1862 words, transcribed from the 1919 Brown Book page scan (No. 8, in A♭; transcription saved as scores/b8/scan/battle_cry_1919.ly) and checked note by note. The chorus ('The Union forever...') is left out: that songbook prints altered chorus words, and no other public-domain score of it was found to check against. No simplification needed. D drum: as written (range low 3 to 3), D minLayout 15. C drum: the C drum has no low 3/4, so 'Shouting the battle' (both times) is played one octave higher; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
